    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes.\n\nThe change was small and fits the existing structure:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` `readOnly` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing `displayName` as `LastName + \", \" + FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nBecause `displayName` lives on the `Owner` schema (shared by create and get responses) and is computed in the single mapper both responders already use, no responder function or endpoint YAML needed touching. The `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `RespondWithOwnerCreated` path and the `GET` path both now return `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.",
